The seam is in place — `DoSomething` is now virtual, so I can subclass `MockService` and override it. My test goes THROUGH the override and asserts on the value the seam produces.

<tool>submit_test(csharp)</tool>
```csharp
using Xunit;

namespace MockSmoke.Tests;

public class MockServiceTests
{
    private sealed class StubService : MockService
    {
        public override string DoSomething() => "stubbed";
    }

    [Fact]
    public void DoSomething_OverriddenThroughVirtualSeam()
    {
        MockService svc = new StubService();
        Assert.Equal("stubbed", svc.DoSomething());
    }
}
```
